    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="1025" n="913" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg913"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-04T14:00:00-04:00">May 4, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your 94, May 2, 5 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d897-f1"/> For your information.
                    According to Standard-Vacuum, New York office of Asiatic Petroleum received from
                    London on May 2 a telegram to the effect that it has also been decided in London
                    that the Asiatic Petroleum should in the first place apply only to Manchuria and
                    should not approach Tokyo unless it later becomes necessary to make a claim.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
